---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="50 Natural Dating Photo Ideas — Dating Photo Lab"
  description="50 simple, realistic photo situations for dating profiles that feel natural, relaxed, and real."
>
  <main>
    <section class="product-hero">
      <div class="product-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">50 PHOTO IDEAS</p>

        <h1>50 Natural Dating Photo Ideas</h1>

        <p class="product-intro">
  50 simple situations to try when you want a photo that feels natural, not
  posed.
</p>

        <a
          class="button"
          href="https://payhip.com/b/T5UHK"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Get the 50 ideas — $5
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="product-introduction">
      <div class="product-introduction-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE IDEA</p>

        <h2>You probably don't need a better camera.</h2>

        <p>
          Most people don't need better cameras or better editing. They just
          need better ideas.
        </p>

        <p>
          A photo can feel awkward simply because there's nothing happening in
          it. These ideas give you something small to do — walking, holding a
          coffee, looking through a book, sitting somewhere, or simply
          pausing for a moment.
        </p>

        <p>
          The goal isn't to make every photo look candid. It's to make the
          moment feel believable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="product-introduction">
      <div class="product-introduction-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">WHAT'S INSIDE</p>

        <h2>50 situations you can actually recreate.</h2>

        <p>
  The ideas range from everyday moments to small movements and simple
  things to do while someone is taking the photo.
</p>

        <div class="product-idea-list">
          <p>01 — Coffee by the Window</p>
          <p>02 — Walking Outside</p>
          <p>03 — Sitting at an Outdoor Café</p>
          <p>04 — Leaning on a Balcony</p>
          <p>05 — Looking Out the Window</p>
          <p>06 — Holding a Book</p>
          <p>07 — Laughing Mid-Moment</p>
          <p>08 — Fixing Hair Naturally</p>
          <p>09 — Walking with Coffee</p>
          <p>10 — Sitting on Stairs</p>
        </div>

        <p class="product-list-note">
          And 40 more simple situations to try.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="product-introduction">
      <div class="product-introduction-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">HOW TO USE IT</p>

        <h2>Start with the situation, not the pose.</h2>

        <p>
          Choose a scene that feels like something you would actually do.
          Then let the action give you something to focus on while someone
          takes the photo.
        </p>

        <p>
          A little movement, some context, or a small thing to hold can change
          the whole feeling of a picture.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="product-closing">
      <p class="eyebrow">ONE SMALL SHIFT</p>

      <h2>Don't search for the perfect pose. Start with something to do.</h2>

      <a
        class="button"
        href="https://payhip.com/b/T5UHK"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Get the 50 ideas — $5
      </a>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .product-idea-list {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .product-idea-list p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .product-list-note {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted, #6f6f6f);
  }
</style>